summary: 'Session took the F4 cold-agent-legibility arc from "rig built, nothing signed" to "one gate signed, two gates blocked on verified defects." Wired the CLI arm''s f4Trace emission (it emitted ZERO rows before, so the falsifier''s "both skins independently" clause was structurally unmeasurable), ratified FG-1 in amended form, ran an FG-3 pre-freeze review that found and fixed two defects in the teaching surface, then convened a six-specialist panel that surfaced nine further defects — including one that makes the just-ratified FG-1 criterion unsatisfiable on a stratum FG-4 requires. Net: real forward progress AND the discovery that signing FG-3/FG-4 today would have pre-registered a broken instrument.'
