learnings:
  - PROBE LIVE, DON'T READ. Both FG-3 defects and the worst panel findings were found by running the thing, not by reading the code — the status/ladder contradiction had survived a full design panel, a build, and 656 passing tests. Reading confirms what you already suspect; probing surfaces what you don't.
  - FREEZE THE CARRIER, NOT A PROXY FOR IT. descriptorsId hashed the descriptions while PW-6 had deliberately moved the teaching into the status result. The same error then repeated one level up (the ladders are still unhashed). When a content address is meant to pin 'what was taught', enumerate every artifact that teaches — the id is only as honest as its scope.
  - A CRITERION THAT CANNOT FAIL IS NOT A GATE. 'Zero W3 marks' cannot fire on the MCP arm (resolve unregistered → throws pre-emit; override flags absent from paramsSchema → dropped before the classifier can see them). Security-by-omission is correct as a defense and void as a measurement control — the two roles must be checked separately.
  - MEASUREMENT INSTRUMENTS FAIL TOWARD PASSING. Commander exits before the CLI action handler and MCP throws before tracer.emit, so mistakes made REACHING the engine are invisible. The measured median is 'wasted turns among calls that reached the engine' — biased toward passing, monotonically with how bad the surface is. Always ask what the instrument CANNOT see.
  - PRE-REGISTERED FALSIFIERS ARBITRATE PANELS. The panel disagreed on sequencing; asking each specialist to name the observation that would falsify their own recommendation meant the disagreement resolved mechanically when the probe tripped two of them. Better than consensus and better than seniority.
  - STATISTICAL POWER IS A PRE-REGISTRATION ITEM. >=10 runs against a >=80% bar gives a Wilson CI of [0.49, 0.94] on 8/10 — it cannot distinguish 0.65 from 0.80. Bars written as round numbers need the arithmetic done BEFORE runs, or the gate is ceremony.
  - VERIFY SUBAGENT FINDINGS BEFORE CEMENTING THEM. Six specialists produced a large surface of claims; re-checking each against the code or live fabric before writing the record kept several severe-sounding but unverified assertions out of the permanent artifact.
